{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Test_scan.Resource_fault_inventory_scan</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"neural_nets_lib","href":"../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Test_scan","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Resource_fault_inventory_scan","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[{"title":"Recognised forms (closed boundary)","href":"#recognised-forms-(closed-boundary)","children":[]}],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>Checking <code>docs/resource-fault-injection-inventory.md</code> against the derived <code>Ir.Resource_fault_injection.point</code> constructors, repository test files, and cited module hooks (gh-ocannl-778).</p><p>Machine-check of <code>docs/resource-fault-injection-inventory.md</code> against the live <code>Ir.Resource_fault_injection.point</code> type, repository test files, and cited module hooks (gh-ocannl-778).</p>","content":"<h2 id=\"recognised-forms-(closed-boundary)\"><a href=\"#recognised-forms-(closed-boundary)\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Recognised forms (closed boundary)</h2><ul><li><b>Table structure</b>: Markdown pipe-table lines (stripped line starting and ending with <code>'|'</code>), skipping the first header row and any separator row whose cells contain only <code>'-'</code>, <code>':'</code>, and whitespace. Every data row must have exactly four pipe-delimited cells (<code>Seam | Failure mode | Status and acceptance evidence | Remaining leg</code>).</li><li><b>Inline code tokens</b>: single-line, single-backtick spans (<code>`...`</code>) inside table data rows. Unclosed backticks on a row are refused; double-backtick fences and prose outside the pipe table are deliberately not read.</li><li><b>Point coverage</b>: the complete constructor set is derived directly from <code>Ir.Resource_fault_injection.all_of_point</code> (never a copied list). Every constructor must appear as a backticked token (<code>`&lt;Point&gt;`</code> or <code>`Resource_fault_injection.&lt;Point&gt;`</code>) in at least one table data row.</li><li><b>Qualified fault-injector references</b>: every backticked token starting with <code>Resource_fault_injection.</code> or <code>FI.</code> in a table row must name a live constructor of <code>all_of_point</code> or a full qualified exported path of <code>arrayjit/lib/resource_fault_injection.mli</code>.</li><li><b>Cited repository paths</b>: every backticked token in a table row containing <code>'/'</code> and ending in <code>&quot;.ml&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;.mli&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;.md&quot;</code>, or <code>&quot;.sh&quot;</code> must exist in the repository's <code>Source_inventory</code>.</li><li><b>Covered-row test requirement</b>: every data row whose <code>Status and acceptance evidence</code> cell starts with <code>&quot;Covered&quot;</code> must cite at least one existing <code>&quot;.ml&quot;</code> test file under <code>&quot;test/&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;arrayjit/test/&quot;</code> in that cell.</li><li><b>Cited <code>Autotune.*</code> hooks</b>: every backticked token starting with <code>&quot;Autotune.&quot;</code> in a table row must name a full qualified value, module, type, or exception path (including nested submodules such as <code>Autotune.Seam.&lt;name&gt;</code>) declared in <code>arrayjit/lib/autotune.mli</code> (parsed via <code>Ppxlib.Parse.interface</code>).</li></ul><p>Deliberately out of scope: relative Markdown links (enforced by <code>markdown_links</code>), prose outside the pipe table, bare unbackticked identifiers, and runtime test execution.</p><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-finding\"><a href=\"#type-finding\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> finding</span><span> = </span></code><ol><li id=\"type-finding.Malformed_row\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-finding.Malformed_row\" class=\"anchor\"></a><c